@startuml B01-cancellation-gap
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF9C4

title B-01 — The Cancellation Gap\nServiceRequest is revoked; the Task owner does not know

actor "Initiating\nFacility" as initiator #FFF9C4
actor "Receiving\nFacility" as receiver  #FFE0CC
actor "Patient" as patient               #C8E6C9
database "FHIR Server" as server         #E3F2FD

autonumber

initiator -> server  : POST ServiceRequest (status=active)
server    --> initiator : SR/cardio-001

initiator -> server  : POST Task (status=requested, focus=SR/cardio-001)
server    --> initiator : Task/track-001

receiver  -> server  : PUT Task/track-001\n(status=accepted, owner=Org/manila-gen\nbusinessStatus=#accepted)
server    --> receiver : 200 OK

note over receiver
  Manila General assigns care navigator.
  Books clinic slot for patient.
  Prepares cardiology consult.
end note

patient   -> initiator : "I changed my mind. I don't want the referral."

initiator -> server  : PUT ServiceRequest/cardio-001\n**status = revoked**
server    --> initiator : 200 OK

note over initiator, server #FFCCCC
  No cascade to Task/track-001.
  No notification to Org/manila-gen.
  No FHIR Subscription defined in the IG.
  No polling requirement specified.
end note

receiver  -> server  : GET Task?owner=Org/manila-gen&status=accepted
server    --> receiver : Task/track-001 (status=accepted)

note over receiver #FFCCCC
  Manila General sees: "Referral accepted."
  Does NOT see: "Referral revoked."

  To detect revocation, receiver would need to:
  GET ServiceRequest/cardio-001
  → discover status=revoked

  This requires out-of-band coordination
  or proactive polling — neither is
  specified in the IG.
end note

receiver  -> patient : SMS: "Your appointment is confirmed at Manila General."
patient   -> receiver : No-show

note right of patient #FFCCCC
  Patient was told referral was cancelled.
  Receiving facility had no idea.
  Clinical capacity wasted.
end note

@enduml
